{
  "_comment": "Bundled model registry (data corpus, NOT a live fetch). One row per model id describing its provider, context window, max output, modalities, capabilities, and approximate public USD/1M-token costs (input/output/cache-write/cache-read). It LAYERS the richer catalog metadata on top of llm/pricing.py's PRICES table: pricing.cost_for / provider_for / pricing_source still fall back to the in-code PRICES + tier heuristic, so this file is purely additive and editable without a code change. The optional base_url lets an OpenAI-compatible self-hosted/aggregator endpoint (vLLM/Ollama/OpenRouter/Together/Groq) be addressed by model id when the per-role ModelConfig cannot carry one. Costs are approximate list prices in USD per 1,000,000 tokens; edit to match your contract or layer a PriceOverlayStore override on top.",
